  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Preguntas en estilo indirecto**",
      "",
      "| Tipo | Directo | Indirecto |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| **Wh-** | *'Where **do** you live?'* | *She asked **where I lived**.* |",
      "| **Sí/no** | *'**Are** you ready?'* | *She asked **if / whether** I **was** ready.* |",
      "",
      "**Reglas**",
      "",
      "- **Orden afirmativo**, sin *do/does/did* ni inversión: ✘ *She asked where did I live* → ✔ *where **I lived***.",
      "- Los tiempos retroceden igual que en las afirmaciones.",
      "- Para preguntas sí/no se usa **if** o **whether** (*whether* es algo más formal, o con *or not*).",
      "- Sin signo de interrogación: *He asked me what time it was.*",
      "",
      "**Órdenes y peticiones**",
      "",
      "| Directo | Indirecto |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| *'Wait here!'* | *She **told** me **to wait** there.* |",
      "| *'Don't touch it.'* | *He **told** me **not to touch** it.* |",
      "| *'Could you open the window?'* | *She **asked** me **to open** the window.* |",
      "",
      "**Estructura:** *tell / ask + persona + (not) to + verbo.*",
      "",
      "**Otras maneras de preguntar de forma indirecta (educada):** *Could you tell me where the station is? · Do you know what time it opens? · I wonder if you could help.* (orden afirmativo).",
      "",
      "**Ojo:** *ask* sirve para preguntar (*ask a question*) y para pedir (*ask for water*). *Ask for* ≠ *ask*. ✘ *She asked me to that I wait*.",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *whether* /ˈweðə/ (th sonora, igual que *weather*) · *references* /ˈrefrənsɪz/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "She asked where did I live.",
        "right": "She asked where I lived.",
        "note": "Sin do/did."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "He told me that wait.",
        "right": "He told me to wait.",
        "note": "Tell + persona + to."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
